-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Monty is Innocent
  Publisher   Gremlin Graphics, 1985
  Version     1.3

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Monty is Innocent (1985)(Gremlin Graphics Software).z80
  MD5         cc90fbe7e7b6568e5f9d00c3226f215b

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Changes     1.1: Starts with the Next's DivMMC automap switched off:
              NextZXOS leaves it on, and on current cores that could crash the
              game or spoil its drawing
              1.2: a guard the gun catches now disappears at once; before, its
              sprite stayed on the screen until the next room
              1.3: Keeps the CPU speed you chose (F8): the sprite updates used
              to drop the Next back to 3.5 MHz

  Note        Keys: on the game's menu 1 to 3 choose the controls. Sam Stoat,
              Monty and the guards are hardware sprites over the pixels the
              game still draws: the guards in their own colours, Sam and Monty
              in white, so the coloured blocks each guard painted around
              itself are gone and nobody changes colour near a guard. Panel
              icons and the items in the rooms stay as the game draws them.
              The added work runs at 28 MHz; about 3% more per frame at the
              original speed.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Guards do not catch you

  From an archive .pok, each checked against this release's code: the lives
  counter's DEC A made OR A (the count is kept), and the guard collision
  test's death routine starts with RET, so the test returns as if Monty had
  not been caught.

