-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      1.2: Tang FPGA board: 1.1 plays from the menu into the prison
              with automap off at start; 1.2 changes only the gun's guard
              erase, verified against the recording and unit cases; NexClash
              differential verification against a 6,241-frame recording; Tang
              FPGA board: loads with DivMMC automap on and sprites left by
              another program and runs its menu (the board's key input did not
              get past the menu, as with Monty on the Run); that board run was
              on the build before a speed-up of the sprite code, which the
              verification covers. Played by the owner on a ZX Spectrum Next
              (KS3), 2026-11-27: good.

  Replay      IDENTICAL on a 6,241-frame recording through 38 screen clears:
              at every hook and every painter call original and patched code
              compared from the same state (every register but R, all 48K
              RAM), every figure's XOR pixels against its four sprites after
              each of 7,531 figure plots (1.0 million pixels); 328 unit cases;
              6 deliberately broken builds rejected

  Hardware    ZX Spectrum Next (Kickstarter 3), System/Next 26.11a: played by
              the owner, good

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
